{
  "slug": "domain-randomisation-range-robustness",
  "direction": "How wide should domain randomisation be? Train a small policy (e.g. cross-entropy method or a tiny policy gradient on CartPole / Pendulum from gymnasium classic control) under different randomisation ranges of physical parameters (mass, length, force), then evaluate on in-range and out-of-range dynamics. Is there a range beyond which nominal performance drops faster than robustness improves? Compare no randomisation, narrow, wide, and a simple automatic curriculum that widens the range on success.",
